style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qS368iXcUvk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 7. <b>Attack on Quidditch's </b><b>World Cup</b><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tsJ1SmAD55Y\" data-code=\"tsJ1SmAD55Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tsJ1SmAD55Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-26-2016, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:45:29-07:00","id":958171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening#post958095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://blaber.pl/rozrywka/geek/harry-potter-mroczne-momenty/\" target=\"_blank\">Here is article in Polish i took clips below from.</a> Videos are in English so should be understandable to all forum users.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Horcrux is basically Soul Stone in <b>Mage</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not even close. It is much closer to things like the Nine Rings from LotR, the needle in which Koschei the Deathless keeps his soul/life, or Lich's Phylacteries from D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I can't see any Potter/Awakening comparisons, because both are so ingrained with their respective magical systems, and they are just SO different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:48:35-07:00","id":958172,"title":"","content":"Soul Stone vs Horcrux? They are totally the same - Item of power that sustains both power and ghost of the creator. Maybe Rowling creation is bit too much, but they works more or less the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:52:01-07:00","id":958174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=958172#post958172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Stone vs Horcrux? They are totally the same - Item of power that sustains both power and ghost of the creator. Maybe Rowling creation is bit too much, but they works more or less the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A Soul Stone is something you take out of yourself, to mostly use as a focus to make magic stronger in a place (or in 1e, direct magic). It's slightly damaging, but (especially in 2e) not that big of a deal<br /> <br /> A Horcrux is a magical imprint on an object that allows you to return from the grave, and is an act of incredibly black magic, requiring the sacrifice of another and the maiming of self.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, both are soul-imprints on objects, but that is where the similarities end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:53:39-07:00","id":958175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=958174#post958174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, both are soul-imprints on objects, but that is where the similarities end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside creation, they work more or less the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:59:04-07:00","id":958176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=958175#post958175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beside creation, they work more or less the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They don't.<br /> <br /> When does a Horcrux create a zone of magical power? When does a Soulstone by itself allow a Mage to return from the grave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:12:58-07:00","id":958179,"title":"","content":"Both are drawn from similar tropes, so there are going to be similarities. That said, are they identical? Nope.<br /> <br /> Harry Potter and Mage are both about wars between &quot;good&quot; wizards and power hungry / evil wizards. How the black hats and not-black-hats manifest are different. Comparisons are inevitable, as are differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:49:17-07:00","id":958318,"title":"","content":"Potter wasn't written based upon the Mage rules so it isn't going to be the same, but that doesn't mean there aren't similarities or more importantly, ideas to be mined from the books/movies. The Horcrux may not be the same as a Soul Stone but Soul Stones can teach legacies and we already have one example were the final attainment turns the recipient into a copy of the original Mage (think of the Chamber of Secrets and what happened to Ginny, minus it actually being a permanent soul change of course). The Death Eaters could be used as inspiration for a legacy of Reapers and if we follow Voldimort's example a Lich Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:14:41-07:00","id":959256,"title":"","content":"I would say a Horcrux is a Soul Stone that is messed with using left handed Death magic, somehow using human souls to fuel esotetic effects like becoming whatever kind of Lich that Lord V is. For sure, if I were to make a Horcrux or Phylactery in the ChroD, id say its something added to/done to a Soulstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:03:49-07:00","id":959336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=959256#post959256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say a Horcrux is a Soul Stone that is messed with using left handed Death magic, somehow using human souls to fuel esotetic effects like becoming whatever kind of Lich that Lord V is. For sure, if I were to make a Horcrux or Phylactery in the ChroD, id say its something added to/done to a Soulstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in HP, dividing the soul requires killing someone. Maybe making a Horcrux works similarly to making a soul stone, but instead of permanently decreasing your maximum Gnosis, it requires decreasing your maximum Wisdom. It's made at the time of a Wisdom drop, and the lost dot can never be recovered. Murder isn't actually the only Act of Hubris that can &quot;divide the soul&quot; in this way, just the most well-known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:11:20-07:00","id":959395,"title":"","content":"You know what works similarly to what you described?<br /> Inuring spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:11:41-07:00","id":959396,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to agree with the thesis with the soul stone and horcrux comparisons and in fact I'd say that LofR example of the One Ring being a soul stone is not too far off the nose.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Sauron for a moment. He was a mortal~ish? (Kind of confused whether he was an angel or mortal race) That crafted powerful artifacts and gave them as poison gifts to his allies. And using those rings he controlled them on his march of conquest. In battle he died, but due to his OneRing never truly being destroyed (I'm looking at you Man) His soul never died. Then he became a Disjoint Eye. Far removed from mortal experiences. I'd say that is a cracked and broken state. And if he ever got his OneRing back he'd be whole and unstoppable.<br /> <br /> It's the Lich's phylactery, how you model it is up to you. And with Awakening starting as a soul stone is not too far off. As long as there's a interesting Mystery and story to go with it. I'd think you'd have good game.<br /> <br /> And as Charlaquin has presented there is design space to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:25:43-07:00","id":959407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=959395#post959395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what works similarly to what you described?<br /> Inuring spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. So, maybe the Horcrux is like a means of Inuring yourself to death (the cessation of life, not the Arcanum).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:57:57-07:00","id":959571,"title":"","content":"In the case of Mage I have to wonder if the act of killing another would be less about splitting your own soul, something the game lets you do totally on your own, and more to do with a Reaper practice of using the victim's soul in the act of creation. Perhaps it would be better explained, within the confines of the game, that the creator uses his victim's soul as a way to give the stone a complete soul of its own. Making it far more than just a fragment of his own. Then if the creator were to die the soul of the stone, which has been shaped to replicate his own, can posses a new form in effect recreating its maker. I like the idea of sacrificing Wisdom instead of Gnosis in its creation, it fits more with the powerful monster that seeks to live forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:13:19-07:00","id":1131603,"title":"","content":"Some very interesting dark <a href=\"http://www.boredpanda.com/harry-potter-redrawn-dark-covers-dylan-pierpont/\" target=\"_blank\">twisted posters of books and movies</a>, showing how much Potter universe is align with Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Part 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Scary Potter &amp; The Sorcerer\u2019s Stone</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static.boredpanda.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/harry-potter-redrawn-dark-covers-dylan-pierpont-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> <b>Scary Potter &amp; The Chamber Of Secrets</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input ty