ze: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static.boredpanda.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/harry-potter-redrawn-dark-covers-dylan-pierpont-7.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b</div></div> </div> </div></b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:38:45-07:00","id":1131731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=959336#post959336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in HP, dividing the soul requires killing someone. Maybe making a Horcrux works similarly to making a soul stone, but instead of permanently decreasing your maximum Gnosis, it requires decreasing your maximum Wisdom. It's made at the time of a Wisdom drop, and the lost dot can never be recovered. Murder isn't actually the only Act of Hubris that can &quot;divide the soul&quot; in this way, just the most well-known.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made rules for Horcruxes a ways back if you're interested. Text is below, and the rest of my Harry Potter/Mage conversion can be found in my signature. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Horcruxes</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Horcruxes are metaphysically similar to Soul Stones, and creating a Horcrux uses the same process as creating a Soul Stone with the following differences:</span></span><ul><li>Creating a Horcrux is not itself an Act of Hubris, but its creation requires Wisdom degeneration caused by spell induced murder. If the murder does not cause degeneration, then the wizard has felt too much remorse to successfully create a Horcrux.</li> <li>If a wizard creates a Horcrux and is later killed, neither their soul nor identity passes on, the wizard instead becoming a twilight being that can be communicated with via the Death or Mind arcana. It loses access to its own Arcana until a body is created for it to inhabit.</li> <li>Because Horcruxes are meant to hold the identity of the creator, holding a Horcrux for more than a scene warps the emotional reactions of the bearer, bringing them in sympathy with the creator of the Horcrux.</li> <li>Horcruxes have none of the features or abilities of Soul Stones, such as Demesne Creation, listed on M2E 98.</li> <li>Horcruxes reduce Wisdom potential instead of Gnosis potential.</li> <li>Destroying a Horcrux restores the lost Wisdom potential (though not the Wisdom dot itself), but reduces the owner\u2019s Gnosis by one dot. This loss of Gnosis does not cause the wizard to lose access to any the Arcana, but if the wizard has Arcana exceeding Gnosis limits, no more Arcana can be learned until the Gnosis rating is restored.</li> <li>The only way to regain the Wisdom and Gnosis lost from a destroyed Horcrux is to assign \u201cRemorse\u201d as an Obsession for an entire Story and the expenditure of 2 Arcane Experience.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:43:50-07:00","id":1131779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1131731#post1131731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made rules for Horcruxes a ways back if you're interested. Text is below, and the rest of my Harry Potter/Mage conversion can be found in my signature. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Horcruxes</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Horcruxes are metaphysically similar to Soul Stones, and creating a Horcrux uses the same process as creating a Soul Stone with the following differences:</span></span><ul><li>Creating a Horcrux is not itself an Act of Hubris, but its creation requires Wisdom degeneration caused by spell induced murder. If the murder does not cause degeneration, then the wizard has felt too much remorse to successfully create a Horcrux.</li> <li>If a wizard creates a Horcrux and is later killed, neither their soul nor identity passes on, the wizard instead becoming a twilight being that can be communicated with via the Death or Mind arcana. It loses access to its own Arcana until a body is created for it to inhabit.</li> <li>Because Horcruxes are meant to hold the identity of the creator, holding a Horcrux for more than a scene warps the emotional reactions of the bearer, bringing them in sympathy with the creator of the Horcrux.</li> <li>Horcruxes have none of the features or abilities of Soul Stones, such as Demesne Creation, listed on M2E 98.</li> <li>Horcruxes reduce Wisdom potential instead of Gnosis potential.</li> <li>Destroying a Horcrux restores the lost Wisdom potential (though not the Wisdom dot itself), but reduces the owner\u2019s Gnosis by one dot. This loss of Gnosis does not cause the wizard to lose access to any the Arcana, but if the wizard has Arcana exceeding Gnosis limits, no more Arcana can be learned until the Gnosis rating is restored.</li> <li>The only way to regain the Wisdom and Gnosis lost from a destroyed Horcrux is to assign \u201cRemorse\u201d as an Obsession for an entire Story and the expenditure of 2 Arcane Experience.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T23:25:39-07:00","id":1132099,"title":"","content":"I do love the line of discussion going on right now. I'd personally constitute the creation of a Horcrux as an Act of Hubris because...come on, Big V's hubris was a core part of the book series. Other than that though, excellent work on that write up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other fun parallels that I personally draw from the series are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Utilizing the internal bureaucracy and politics of the Ministry of Magic as a template for Consili politics in particularly ancient Consilia. (Because who in Pentacle politics hasn't covered up the return of a dangerous Left-Handed Legacy for fear of losing their hard fought influence and resources within the Awakened community. Besides, their founder was killed. It's not like he could come back to life or something, best not to cause an unnecessary panic.) <br /> <br /> \u2022 Drawing inspiration from a number of the book's miscellaneous wizarding wonders for magical artifacts or enchanted items (from loveably harmless to mind shatteringly deadly.)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Drawing inspiration from Hogwarts legends and in world folklore to create Mysteries (Secret pathways and tunnels everywhere, rooms that appear only when needed, ancient revenge plots, lingering ghosts with tragic secrets, secret civilizations in the woods and lake, Hogwarts would be a Mysyery addict's dreamland.)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Drawing inspiration from the book's magical orders and traditions for Legacies (Death Eaters, Aurers, Animagus, hell even the Weasly Twin's could be inspiration for a Legacy of Awakened tricksters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T23:34:33-07:00","id":1132102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1131731#post1131731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made rules for Horcruxes a ways back if you're interested. Text is below, and the rest of my Harry Potter/Mage conversion can be found in my signature. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Horcruxes</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Horcruxes are metaphysically similar to Soul Stones, and creating a Horcrux uses the same process as creating a Soul Stone with the following differences:</span></span><ul><li>Creating a Horcrux is not itself an Act of Hubris, but its creation requires Wisdom degeneration caused by spell induced murder. If the murder does not cause degeneration, then the wizard has felt too much remorse to successfully create a Horcrux.</li> <li>If a wizard creates a Horcrux and is later killed, neither their soul nor identity passes on, the wizard instead becoming a twilight being that can be communicated with via the Death or Mind arcana. It loses access to its own Arcana until a body is created for it to inhabit.</li> <li>Because Horcruxes are meant to hold the identity of the creator, holding a Horcrux for more than a scene warps the emotional reactions of the bearer, bringing them in sympathy with the creator of the Horcrux.</li> <li>Horcruxes have none of the features or abilities of Soul Stones, such as Demesne Creation, listed on M2E 98.</li> <li>Horcruxes reduce Wisdom potential instead of Gnosis potential.</li> <li>Destroying a Horcrux restores the lost Wisdom potential (though not the Wisdom dot itself), but reduces the owner\u2019s Gnosis by one dot. This loss of Gnosis does not cause the wizard to lose access to any the Arcana, but if the wizard has Arcana exceeding Gnosis limits, no more Arcana can be learned until the Gnosis rating is restored.</li> <li>The only way to regain the Wisdom and Gnosis lost from a destroyed Horcrux is to assign \u201cRemorse\u201d as an Obsession for an entire Story and the expenditure of 2 Arcane Experience.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm planning to go a different route with my HP/MtAw crossover for Horcruxes, but this is awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:47:37-07:00","id":1132142,"title":"","content":"It's also interesting how inuring yourself to murder prevents horcrux creation. I'm not entirely sure that <i>feels</i> right, but it makes sense from a metaphysical perspective because you've basically made your soul immune to the the damage that creation of a horcrux requires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T11:12:26-07:00","id":1132304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=959256#post959256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say a Horcrux is a Soul Stone that is messed with using left handed Death magic, somehow using human souls to fuel esotetic effects like becoming whatever kind of Lich that Lord V is. For sure, if I were to make a Horcrux or Phylactery in the ChroD, id say its something added to/done to a Soulstone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ExactlyWhatItSaysOnTheTin\" target=\"_blank\">Cleverest of Things</a> indeed, That is a <i>great</i> Reaper Lich Legacy Idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=959571#post959571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In the case of Mage I have to wonder if the act of killing another would be less about splitting your own soul, something the game lets you do totally on your own, and more to do with a Reaper practice of using the victim's soul in the act of creation. Perhaps it would be better explained, within the confines of the game, that the creator uses his victim's soul as a way to give the stone a complete soul of its own. Making it far more than just a fragment of his own. Then if the creator were to die the soul of the stone, which has been shaped to replicate his own, can posses a new form in effect recreating its maker. I like the idea of sacrificing Wisdom instead of Gnosis in its creation, it fits more with the powerful monster that seeks to live forever.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, expansion of the previous idea with more details. Since it is possible to steal souls without murder but murder can be its own supernatural power source (Via the principles that power Devour the Slain MtA p.130), it may a combination of harvesting and the use of a Soul specifically through murder that allows to formation of a Horcrux-like Soul Stone that grants immortality. It may very well be that it requires murder so the fuel source reshaping the Soul has the proper Resonance (What Mana source has a more perfect synchronized Resonance with a Soul than Mana extracted from the source of the Soul? Especially since they are both gathered up at the same moment making Temporal Sympathy also aligned as well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:54:00-07:00","id":1132862,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that you also have to do something so terrible after the murder that JK won't even describe it to Big V's actor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T04:58:47-07:00","id":1132967,"title":"","content":"More like so terrible she didn't actually come up with anything specific, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:30:52-07:00","id":1133257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1132967#post1132967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like so terrible she didn't actually come up with anything specific, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like it, but I have to acknowledge it as a sick burn. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't think it's necrophilia. Far too crude for both Voldy and JK","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:44:15-07:00","id":1133261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1133257#post1133257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like it, but I have to acknowledge it as a sick burn. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't think it's necrophilia. Far too crude for both Voldy and JK</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be a burn. I had the same thought, that she likely never addressed it, but that could be because the horrible thing left unsaid is almost always more terrible than the thing you know happened. <br /> <br /> Almost. Please no one try to prove me wrong, my brain isn't up for that right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T03:20:43-07:00","id":1133313,"title":"","content":"Also this does raise the question of how exactly he managed to turn Harry into one <i>accidentally</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:02:14-07:00","id":1133430,"title":"","content":"Intriguing conversation, and the Horcrux example is very interesting and usable!<br /> <br /> \u200bI recently had some idle thoughts whilst watching the young-uns on vacation (in Toronto of all places, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>):<br /> <br /> What if the wizards of the HP-verse are all Proximi? Descended from (five) very powerful lines (read: a wide range of rotes) that tended to breed true--sparked perhaps by the Holy Grail (and/or other Supernal sources). The five founders of Hogwarts, realizing that the proximi wizardlings needed instruction in order to wisely use their gifts, as well as to prepare should any awake to True Magic, established their school. The Sorting Hat's main task is to identify which of the five major lines a young student is most linked to, given the extensive blood mixing by modern days, and assigns them to the House that will most support their potential.<br /> <br /> The rest of the setting, such as the Ministry of Magic, the international diaspora of wizards (versus true Mages), and the like spring from support by both the Diamond and Seers to ensure that the more-numerous wizard proximi don't do irreparable damage to mortal fabrics.<br /> <br /> Um... discuss?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. I've seen the films but not read the books. Be gentle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:12:24-07:00","id":1133576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1133430#post1133430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intriguing conversation, and the Horcrux example is very interesting and usable!<br /> <br /> \u200bI recently had some idle thoughts whilst watching the young-uns on vacation (in Toronto of all places, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>):<br /> <br /> What if the wizards of the HP-verse are all Proximi? Descended from (five) very powerful lines (read: a wide range of rotes) that tended to breed true--sparked perhaps by the Holy Grail (and/or other Supernal sources). The five founders of Hogwarts, realizing that the proximi wizardlings needed instruction in order to wisely use their gifts, as well as to prepare should any awake to True Magic, established their school. The Sorting Hat's main task is to identify which of the five major lines a young student is most linked to, given the extensive blood mixing by modern days, and assigns them to the House that will most support their potential.<br /> <br /> The rest of the setting, such as the Ministry of Magic, the international diaspora of wizards (versus true Mages), and the like spring from support by both the Diamond and Seers to ensure that the more-numerous wizard proximi don't do irreparable damage to mortal fabrics.<br /> <br /> Um... discuss?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. I've seen the films but not read the books. Be gentle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really neat idea! It would be an interesting and very different take on the HP world, but it could work.<br /> <br /> Also, you really should read the books. They are wonderful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T18:19:03-07:00","id":1133615,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's my crack at figuring out the arcana for each house. This is just spitballing and very rough, so it may not be as internally consistent as I'd like. <br /> <br /> <b>Gryffindor</b>: Life, Matter, Spirit (Path: Thyrsus) <br /> <b>Hufflepuff</b>: Fate, Life, Time (Path: Acanthus) <br /> <b>Peverell</b>: Death, Forces, Matter (Path: Moros)<br /> <b>Ravenclaw</b>: Forces, Mind, Prime (Path: Obrimos) <br /> <b>Slytherin</b>: Fate, Mind, Space (Path: Mastigos) <br /> <br /> If I get some time, I may try to do a more detailed write-up of each. While I'm going to stick with using full-on mages for my version of Harry &amp; co, it did help me a plot point later on, so thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:46:05-07:00","id":1133750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1133615#post1133615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's my crack at figuring out the arcana for each house. This is just spitballing and very rough, so it may not be as internally consistent as I'd like.<br /> <br /> <b>Gryffindor</b>: Life, Matter, Spirit (Path: Thyrsus)<br /> <b>Hufflepuff</b>: Fate, Life, Time (Path: Acanthus)<br /> <b>Peverell</b>: Death, Forces, Matter (Path: Moros)<br /> <b>Ravenclaw</b>: Forces, Mind, Prime (Path: Obrimos)<br /> <b>Slytherin</b>: Fate, Mind, Space (Path: Mastigos)<br /> <br /> If I get some time, I may try to do a more detailed write-up of each. While I'm going to stick with using full-on mages for my version of Harry &amp; co, it did help me a plot point later on, so thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> ! I'll probably read the books when the little ones are old enough to appreciate them. Part of this idea sprung from a few observations: <br /> <br /> 1) It seems like there are a lot of wizards in the HP-verse.<br /> 2) Their spells are nearly always consistent formula that do pretty much that one thing per design; application has a bit of flexibility however.<br /> 3) They use magic for a great deal of casual &quot;technology&quot; that would get a mage into trouble with his Wisdom....<br /> 4) No one seems concerned about paradox (obviously).<br /> 5) They're super-worried about training youngsters right, which is a matter of blood potential and not the result of anything like strange astral quests.<br /> <br /> This, to me, points toward Proximi, and by necessity Proximi with perhaps a greater range of rotes. Greater Proximi maybe? Permitting lesser mud-blood characters to take the cheaper Proximi merits?<br /> <br /> Someplace on the interwebs there is probably a mapping of HP spells to Mage effects, but I haven't looked yet. Other than an academic-ish interest, any application of this sort of mash-up would come much later in my own plots. But I do enjoy mixing in other materials whenever possible.<br /> <br /> A further note: the wizarding world's luminaries are likely True Mages. This would include Dumbledore, Voldemort and probably Harry after the experiences of the books. This would explain how, for example, Voldemort could get away with causing such trouble and the Consilium didn't/couldn't squash him flat. Sirius Black might be a Storyteller-approved mixing of Proximi and werewolf, or have a moon-change curse (Tell?). I'm just scratching the surface of course.<br /> <br /> The point being that you can insert an intermediate layer of secrecy in-between the Diamond-Nameless-Seers world of madness and Truth (capital T), and the mundane, muggle world that struggles not to see the darkness around the edges. <br /> <br /> It's a potentially useful distinction.<br /> <br /> \u200b--Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T06:36:43-07:00","id":1133765,"title":"","content":"You mean Lupin. Lupins the werewolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:22:33-07:00","id":1133826,"title":"","content":"Sirius could have the tell that lets you turn into a regular wolf whenever you want to. Remus gets the one that forces you into Urshul on the full moon.<br /> <br /> 'Course, Animagi actually work most like a legacy. It's a self-targeted transfiguration spell that they can just <i>do </i>at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:14:31-07:00","id":1135318,"title":"","content":"Well if Animagi are a Legacy, (and we a r ea bit playful) then perhaps Harry is on the first step of a Left-Handed Reaper Legacy. (Has a soulstone bonded to his flesh), which was thrust upon him when He-Should-Now-Be-Named failed to kill him. Would provide story mechanic for why Dumbledor might need him to unlock some of the different dark wizard hide-aways? And HArry is technically short one soulstone since his thoughts can be opened through the Sympathy of the soul shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:26:48-07:00","id":1135321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135318#post1135318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if Animagi are a Legacy, (and we a r ea bit playful) then perhaps Harry is on the first step of a Left-Handed Reaper Legacy. (Has a soulstone bonded to his flesh), which was thrust upon him when He-Should-Now-Be-Named failed to kill him. Would provide story mechanic for why Dumbledor might need him to unlock some of the different dark wizard hide-aways? And HArry is technically short one soulstone since his thoughts can be opened through the Sympathy of the soul shard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Voldemort's Horcrux is less of a legacy and more of a curse, or even more accurately, a Destiny with some added perks and drawbacks from other Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:09:17-07:00","id":1135394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1133750#post1133750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It seems like there are a lot of wizards in the HP-verse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that they have a much more connected society and it tends to concentrate in certain places. Like, there's one school for the UK and everyone goes there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Greater Proximi maybe? Permitting lesser mud-blood characters to take the cheaper Proximi merits? </div> </div> </div>To clarify a little, it's a major plot point that magic isn't exactly tied to blood potential. 'Mud-blood' is explicitly meant to be a term of quasi-racist abuse. The race purists are the bad guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:36:13-07:00","id":1135399,"title":"","content":"IIRC it was implied later that most muggle-born wizards have a squib somewhere in their ancestry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:10:20-07:00","id":1135413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135399#post1135399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was implied later that most muggle-born wizards have a squib somewhere in their ancestry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, which is my basis for understanding their world. In other words: there is a reason why a given kid is going to turn up as a wizard, and if your parents are/were wizards there is darn good reason to keep an eye on you and develop the talents you're expected to have in a formal way. If the magical society lost its notes on your ancestry then a Sorting Hat makes real sense.<br /> <br /> The blood-lineage of magic... all actually bolsters the moral position of the heroes, in that they are acting to underline the <i>fundamental humanity</i> of wizards and muggles together, regardless of achievement or special abilities. They do this in the face of objective evidence of the superiority of their &quot;line&quot;, so to speak, insomuch as they have super powers. Along a similar vein the Death Eaters are reprehensible but not insane: their quest for purity makes (some) sense if your objective is elevating magic over humanity. Note: &quot;some&quot; -- Hermione is explicitly elevated as one of the foremost wizards of the next generation to illustrate that &quot;purity&quot; ain't all that important compared to other factors.<br /> <br /> Nasty race-purists in the real world can be scoffed at as silly (if scary) fools and withstood on moral grounds at the same time. A two-fer.<br /> Nasty race-purists in a fantasy world have a point and <i><b>that makes the moral stand much more telling</b></i>. This is salient for all of the CofD setting in which the supernatural is natural.<br /> <br /> Anyway, going back to the discussion of merits (versus the merits of discussion): if you wanted to minimize the influence of degrees of blood-connection then have no lesser/greater Proximi status. &quot;Greater&quot; Proximi was intended as an observation that the usual set of Proximi Rote access seemed a tad small for properly portraying HP-verse wizards at the height of their learned power.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:20:32-07:00","id":1135416,"title":"","content":"I do agree that if we're doing HP wizards as proximi they'll need a buff. The current version is a bit too limited.<br /> <br /> So, Greater Proximi: I'm thinking having their blessings go all the way up to 5 dot spells is a good start. Maybe nix the &quot;paradox ruins spells&quot; thing too, so they can be looser with reach.<br /> <br /> Oh, what if they could learn attainments as sort of pseudo-blessings? Would that break anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-30-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:38:47-07:00","id":1135418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135399#post1135399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was implied later that most muggle-born wizards have a squib somewhere in their ancestry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Well that sours a lot of happy childhood memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:42:13-07:00","id":1135420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135418#post1135418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Well that sours a lot of happy childhood memories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They probably had mostly muggle relatives though. It's also implied that if wizards had only married wizards, they would have died out from inbreeding centuries ago and that the strength of your magic is entirely reliant on skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:00:16-07:00","id":1135430,"title":"","content":"Note she said <i>most</i>, not all.<br /> <br /> Magic likely does pop up out of absolutely nowhere on occasion (it's probably where the first wizards and witches came from) but it's more common for it to be a latent trait that resurfaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:18:42-07:00","id":1135435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135430#post1135430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note she said <i>most</i>, not all.<br /> <br /> Magic likely does pop up out of absolutely nowhere on occasion (it's probably where the first wizards and witches came from) but it's more common for it to be a latent trait that resurfaced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, the whole point of a magic-verse is that there are free radicals out there that spark capabilities and events in non-deterministic ways. In the supposition of wizards as Proximi lines, something had to start that, but across the world that spark would not be the same nor occur at the same time. The Supernal moves in mysterious ways....<br /> <br /> I defer to the collective wisdom when it comes to adjusting Proximi, because both my HP-verse and Mage knowledge are limited. That said, if you're effectively re-writing the Mage setting to incorporate a layer of action like this then handing out weaker attainments to reflect, say, HP-verse major houses and their predilections sounds fine.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:11:00-07:00","id":1135455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1135399#post1135399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was implied later that most muggle-born wizards have a squib somewhere in their ancestry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, giving it some more thought, that doesn't really contradict what I said. The point is that pure-bloods think it makes them better at magic and that's pretty clearly not true.<br /> <br /> You don't really need levels of Proximi based on blood purity because that's not a thing in either HP or Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T22:14:20-07:00","id":1138500,"title":"","content":"Another compilation when HP is like MtAw... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QsLTPXfJgCI\" data-code=\"QsLTPXfJgCI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QsLTPXfJgCI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T14:26:08-07:00","id":1138697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958095-when-harry-potter-series-is-really-like-mage-the-awakening?p=1138500#post1138500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another compilation when HP is like MtAw... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you trying to imply that Awakening is just a kids book that was put together with minimal concern for continuity? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />"